{
  "$comment": "How the activity days a range covers fold into the one period a Usage page shows. The website and both Apple apps answer this file. An Account summary folds four periods on the server; any other period is the same days added up, by whichever client is showing it. Token counts add. Cost amounts and row counts add, and the basis and the status then follow from the counts exactly as they do for one row: complete when no row was left unpriced, partial when some were and some were priced, unavailable when none were priced. Two days priced against different catalog revisions name no revision. Unpriced items are merged by (billing_channel, model, reason) and sorted by that triple. A period is incomplete when any day in it is. A folded period carries no agent tree: a day carries one only when it was asked for on its own.",
